    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The kingdom of the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#saxons">Saxons</a>, centred on Winchester, which grew from small beginnings in the upper Thames valley and the Solent region.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> it alone of the English kingdoms survived the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vikings">Viking</a> onslaught, defended by a network of fortified burhs.</li><li>Alfred’s heirs conquered the Danelaw, and in 927 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#aethelstan">Æthelstan</a> made Wessex the core of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#england">England</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#saxons">Saxon</a> Chronicle, first compiled in Wessex in Alfred’s reign, was still being kept up at Peterborough Abbey in 1154.</p></aside>
    </section>

